{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794308408,"nonce":"fKVzsm39M8qughaYqA9x/G87aLM=","title":"A vector Lagrange field next to an N1E field crashes with a reshape error","message":"On the non-nodal assembler a Lagrange field is sized n_verts and gathered by vertex id, i.e. scalar only. A vector P1 field (value_shape=(3,)) beside an N1E field therefore fails in _unpack_components with 'cannot reshape array of shape (4, 1, 3) into shape (4, 3, 3)', linear or nonlinear, instead of being supported or refused by name. Repro: N1E E with curl-curl + mass, scalar P1 T, vector P1 u with a symgrad elasticity term, on a unit box. Workaround: one scalar Lagrange field per component.","files":null}]}